The native backend

The backend is written in small languages: the sources are src/declarative
(lang/ holds the languages; backend/, a64/, x64/, a64-direct/, x64-direct/,
direct/ and cir/ the files written in them). This directory is what Coil
compiles:

  rt/         the runtime the languages' output stands on, written by hand
  adapter/    from the compiler's CIR to the backend, written by hand (the part
              written once for both machines is src/declarative/adapter/machine.coil)
  generated/  what the languages make of the sources, written by
              scripts/compiler/gen-declarative.py. Nothing in generated/ is
              edited by hand; the fast tier fails when it is not what the
              sources say.

Where it comes from

The backend began as coil-stogir (https://github.com/jimmyhmiller/coil-stogir),
a Coil port and adaptation of IR, which it was then rewritten from, language
first, in coil-stogir-declarative
(https://github.com/jimmyhmiller/coil-stogir-declarative). Its graph, the
analyses and passes over it, the split-interval register allocator and its
emission take IR as their reference.

